# Alertmanager's options. Its API takes alerts and silences, so it needs auth of
# its own: --web.config.file points at the exporter-toolkit web config installed
# as /etc/alertmanager/web.yml (basic_auth_users, bcrypt hash), and Prometheus
# authenticates with the matching plaintext from
# /etc/prometheus/alertmanager_password. Both are hand-placed host state, never
# in git. The listener also stays on loopback, so a process off this box cannot
# reach it even with the credential. HA gossip is off (empty
# --cluster.listen-address). fleet-host-config.service installs this file and
# restarts prometheus-alertmanager.service when it changes (ansible/host.yml).
# Silences and the notification log live in the package's state directory,
# which the service user owns.
ARGS="--config.file=/etc/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml --storage.path=/var/lib/prometheus/alertmanager --web.listen-address=127.0.0.1:9093 --cluster.listen-address= --web.config.file=/etc/alertmanager/web.yml"
